  "readmeFile": "PACKAGE.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Minor because a schema-validated node's type annotation changes: a node of a union type is annotated\nwith the union, not with the member its value matched. A host that reads `TypeAnnotation` of such a\nnode sees the union's name. No API is removed or changed; serialized output does not change. The\ndatabase engine's gate on this release candidate (df34ec2) was identical to its 2.5.0 baseline.\n\n- **Documentation: `IDocument` is a handle, not a snapshot.** Its documentation said the document is\n  an immutable snapshot taken when it was retrieved; a read returns one committed version, whole,\n  and which version is the implementation's to define (the engine: the version current when the\n  read starts, or that of the enclosing read transaction). No code changes.\n\n- **An element in several substitution groups (XSD 1.1) loads.** The XSD 1.1 compatibility layer\n  keeps the first head in `substitutionGroup`, which the XSD 1.0 processor reads, and lists every\n  head as expanded names in `urn:phoenixmldb:xsd11-compatibility:substitutionGroups`, an attribute\n  the declaration keeps (`XmlSchemaElement.UnhandledAttributes`). The schema did not compile.\n  Validation sees the first head only. QT3 substitution-020..025, with the XQuery change.\n\n- **Behaviour change: a node validated against a union type is annotated with the union, not with\n  the member type its value matched** (XDM 3.1 §3.3.1.2: the annotation is the governing type).\n  `XmlDocumentParser` passes the union to `SchemaTypeAnnotator`; the annotator computes the typed\n  value, which still comes from the first member the value is valid for. With the member as the\n  annotation, `element(*, M)` matched an element declared with the union type U, and\n  `element(*, U)` relied on union membership to match it. An xs:ID member still makes the content\n  an ID. W3C XSLT match-195, match-211, with the XQuery and XSLT changes.",
